---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import profile from '../assets/images/profile.jpg';
import guitarStage from '../assets/images/guitar-stage.jpg';
import guitarAcoustic from '../assets/images/guitar-acoustic.jpg';
import piano from '../assets/images/piano.jpg';
---

<Layout>
	<section class="intro">
		<Image class="avatar" src={profile} alt="Mayuresh" width={120} height={120} />
		<div>
			<h1>About Me</h1>
			<p class="title">Builder of distributed systems, platforms, and the occasional guitar riff.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="about">
		<p>
			I like building things, understanding how they work, and finding structure in seemingly
			complicated problems.
		</p>

		<p>
			I've spent the last 15 years working across different layers of software&mdash;from mobile
			applications and SDKs to backend systems, distributed platforms, cloud infrastructure, and
			ML platforms. My career has taken me through Samsung, Amazon, and Maersk, where I've had the
			opportunity to work on everything from software running on flagship mobile devices to
			platforms processing millions of requests a day and systems that bring machine learning into
			business workflows.
		</p>

		<p>What has stayed constant is my fascination with <strong>structure</strong>.</p>

		<p>
			I enjoy taking something complex, breaking it down into its fundamental pieces,
			understanding how those pieces interact, and then finding the right abstractions to put it
			back together. That's probably why distributed systems and platform engineering have always
			felt natural to me. Good architecture, to me, is often about discovering the underlying
			structure of a problem and making it simpler for everyone else.
		</p>

		<p>Interestingly, I find the same satisfaction in music.</p>

		<p>
			Music is an incredibly structured system&mdash;notes, scales, intervals, rhythm, harmony and
			patterns all fitting together to create something that feels intuitive and expressive. I
			enjoy exploring that structure through the guitar and piano/keyboard. I'm not trying to be a
			great musician; I simply enjoy being able to pick up an instrument, understand a little more
			of the underlying system, and then use that understanding to make something.
		</p>

		<div class="photo-row">
			<figure>
				<Image src={guitarStage} alt="Playing electric guitar on stage" width={400} height={533} />
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<Image src={piano} alt="Playing piano/keyboard" width={400} height={300} />
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<Image src={guitarAcoustic} alt="Playing acoustic guitar at home" width={400} height={300} />
			</figure>
		</div>

		<p>
			That curiosity extends beyond engineering too. I like learning how things work,
			experimenting with new ideas, and occasionally going down completely unnecessary rabbit
			holes simply because something is interesting.
		</p>

		<h3>Engineering</h3>

		<p>My professional journey has moved across domains rather than staying confined to one layer of the stack.</p>

		<p>
			I started with enterprise backend systems, moved into mobile and SDK development at
			Samsung, then spent several years at Amazon building distributed and ML platforms, and most
			recently worked at Maersk on large-scale logistics platforms, developer platforms, and
			workflow systems.
		</p>

		<p>
			Working across mobile and backend has shaped how I think about software. I've seen problems
			from both ends: the experience of the developer or user consuming a platform, and the
			complexity of the systems underneath it.
		</p>

		<p>
			Today, I'm particularly interested in <strong
				>distributed systems, platform engineering, AI/ML platforms, developer productivity, and
				the architecture that connects all of them</strong
			>.
		</p>

		<p>
			I enjoy problems where the answer isn't obvious&mdash;where you have to understand the
			system, find the real constraint, make the right trade-offs, and build something that gives
			other people leverage.
		</p>

		<p>
			And outside of all of that, you'll probably find me with a guitar, a keyboard, or exploring
			some new idea that I probably didn't need to explore.
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.intro :global(.avatar) {
		width: 90px;
		height: 90px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.intro h1 {
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
	}

	.title {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about h3 {
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}

	.photo-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.photo-row figure {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.photo-row :global(img) {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		border-radius: 8px;
		aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
	}

	@media (max-width: 36rem) {
		.intro {
			flex-direction: column;
			align-items: flex-start;
		}

		.photo-row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}

		.photo-row figure:first-child {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
		}
	}
</style>
